From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rein van der Zee <rvanderzee@victronenergy.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: omap: don't write beyond the end of the rx buffer

omap_i2c_receive_data() copies num_bytes from the RX FIFO into the
message buffer without checking buf_len. For RRDY, num_bytes is the
FIFO threshold, not the number of bytes still expected, so an RRDY
interrupt arriving when the message is already complete writes a full
threshold worth of bytes past the end of the buffer and underflows
buf_len. A following RDR then uses the truncated, underflowed buf_len
as byte count and overwrites even more memory.

On an am62xx Cerbo GX this happens during heavy touch use on 33-byte
touch reads (FIFO threshold 16) and eventually corrupts the stack of
the edt-ft5x06 interrupt thread:

  Kernel panic - not syncing: stack-protector: Kernel stack is
  corrupted in: edt_ft5x06_ts_isr+0x1d8/0x1d8 [edt_ft5x06]

Drain and drop the unexpected bytes instead and warn about it. The
transfer itself is left to complete as before, so the requested data
is still delivered; resetting the controller mid-transfer can leave
other devices on the bus in an undefined state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-omap.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-omap.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-omap.c
index 0bdee43dc134..15d9a1931dab 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-omap.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-omap.c
@@ -193,6 +193,7 @@ struct omap_i2c_dev {
 	u8			*buf;
 	u8			*regs;
 	size_t			buf_len;
+	u16			addr;		/* target of current msg */
 	struct i2c_adapter	adapter;
 	u8			threshold;
 	u8			fifo_size;	/* use as flag and value
@@ -677,6 +678,7 @@ static int omap_i2c_xfer_msg(struct i2c_adapter *adap,
 	/* REVISIT: Could the STB bit of I2C_CON be used with probing? */
 	omap->buf = msg->buf;
 	omap->buf_len = msg->len;
+	omap->addr = msg->addr;
 
 	/* make sure writes to omap->buf_len are ordered */
 	barrier();
@@ -1000,10 +1002,18 @@ static int errata_omap3_i462(struct omap_i2c_dev *omap)
 static void omap_i2c_receive_data(struct omap_i2c_dev *omap, u8 num_bytes,
 		bool is_rdr)
 {
+	unsigned int	dropped = 0;
 	u16		w;
 
 	while (num_bytes--) {
 		w = omap_i2c_read_reg(omap, OMAP_I2C_DATA_REG);
+
+		/* Never write beyond the end of the message buffer */
+		if (!omap->buf_len) {
+			dropped++;
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		*omap->buf++ = w;
 		omap->buf_len--;
 
@@ -1011,11 +1021,17 @@ static void omap_i2c_receive_data(struct omap_i2c_dev *omap, u8 num_bytes,
 		 * Data reg in 2430, omap3 and
 		 * omap4 is 8 bit wide
 		 */
-		if (omap->flags & OMAP_I2C_FLAG_16BIT_DATA_REG) {
+		if ((omap->flags & OMAP_I2C_FLAG_16BIT_DATA_REG) &&
+		    omap->buf_len) {
 			*omap->buf++ = w >> 8;
 			omap->buf_len--;
 		}
 	}
+
+	if (dropped)
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(omap->dev,
+			"%s: dropped %u unexpected RX bytes for addr 0x%02x\n",
+			is_rdr ? "RDR" : "RRDY", dropped, omap->addr);
 }
 
 static int omap_i2c_transmit_data(struct omap_i2c_dev *omap, u8 num_bytes,
